body:
**Labels:** bug, testing

**Problem**

`BenchmarkRegistryByName` and `BenchmarkRegistryAll` in `internal/providers/registry_test.go` both loop 100 times calling `reg.Register(...)` with the **same** `NameVal: "provider"` on every iteration.

```go
for i := 0; i < 100; i++ {
    reg.Register(ProviderConfig{
        NameVal:      "provider",  // ← same name every iteration
        ...
    })
}
```

`ProviderRegistry.Register` calls `getOrCreate(name)` which panics via `log.panicf("providers.Register: %q already registered", name)` when a name is registered twice. As a result both benchmarks crash immediately on the second iteration with:

```
panic: providers.Register: provider \"provider\" already registered
```

**Proposed fix**

Use a unique provider name per iteration:

```go
for i := 0; i < 100; i++ {
    reg.Register(ProviderConfig{
        NameVal:      fmt.Sprintf(\"provider-%d\", i),
        ...
    })
}
```

Apply the same change to `BenchmarkRegistryAll`.
